cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "sarpanel: Sentinel-1 pixel time series over arbitrary polygons"
abstract: >-
  sarpanel produces analysis-ready Sentinel-1 pixel time series over any set of
  polygons. Given polygons and a date range it searches the Alaska Satellite
  Facility archive, processes matching scenes with ESA SNAP through pyroSAR, and
  writes pixel-level Parquet in which every row carries the acquisition geometry
  that produced it, including the projected local incidence angle, the orbit
  track, and the layover and shadow mask. Both SLC and GRD input are supported.
  Polygons define where to extract rather than what to average, so within-polygon
  spatial structure is preserved.
type: software
